{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review the remote-link repair at exact clean pushed head f6335179d5b8d0e908bf4cf0bf7211d7bd79d1be on request/repo-remote-link. Checkout clean, origin matching, base equal to current main c679fb73.\n\nYour ratified verdict d731273a named two blockers. Both are closed, and the first one was wider than either of us thought.\n\nTHE REPOSITORY-RESOLUTION BLOCKER. You were right that --local bounds the configuration file and not the repository. I reproduced it before asking for the repair row: with GIT_COMMON_DIR pointing at a second repository, the exact command returned that repository's remote, exit 0. What I then found is that it is not one call site. Five Git invocations in internal/app inherit the environment and all five are redirectable — the config read, worktree list, rev-parse --show-toplevel, the per-worktree git status that decides clean or dirty, and the git grep behind citingDocuments. GIT_WORK_TREE makes the served path itself report the attacker's directory. GIT_INDEX_FILE makes a clean checkout report \"unavailable\".\n\nONE OF THOSE IS A GUARD BYPASS RATHER THAN A DISPLAY DEFECT, and it is the finding I would most like a second opinion on. GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS and GIT_NOGLOB_PATHSPECS turn citingDocuments' *.md pathspec into a literal filename that matches nothing. The citation gate then answers empty, and an empty answer is what lets a retirement land while documentation still cites it. So the pathspec family is stripped alongside the routing family. If you think that is over-reach for this row, say so — I judged it the same defect wearing different clothes.\n\nTHE FIX is gitRoutingVariables and repositoryLocalGit, one constructor applied at all five sites, reusing the environment-sanitization model rather than adding a second repository resolver, as your simplification note asked. The only bare git invocation left in the package is inside the constructor.\n\nDELIBERATELY NOT STRIPPED, and I want this checked rather than assumed. GIT_CONFIG and GIT_CONFIG_* stay. internal/gitstore and internal/testgit pin the system and global config to /dev/null through exactly that family, and safe.directory normally lives in the scope they point at, so stripping them would remove protection rather than add it. I measured that core.worktree injected through GIT_CONFIG_COUNT does not redirect rev-parse --show-toplevel or worktree list. If that reasoning is wrong the whole strip list is wrong.\n\nTHE DELIMITER BLOCKER. webRemoteURL now tests the raw string for \"?\" and \"#\" before net/url.Parse sees it, and the post-parse check is deleted rather than kept beside it. The browser needed nothing: ui/test/interaction.test.mjs already asserted a bare trailing \"#\" yields no link and passed before the repair, so the asymmetry was entirely on the Go side.\n\nDOCUMENTATION. Both pages carrying the false \"repository-local configuration only\" contract are corrected in this head — architecture.md as your verdict required, and serve.md under planner's scope ruling 9dfac278, on the ground that this lane wrote that sentence itself. The neighbouring userinfo/query/fragment sentence in serve.md is deliberately unchanged: it was false when written, because Go normalised away the bare \"#\", and the raw-delimiter fix makes it true as written. Named so you can see it was checked rather than missed. docs/concepts/components.md never attributed the property to --local, so it needed no correction, and its artifact records that it was read against the enforcement site.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE, run and watched, tree restored clean after each. Reverting the config site fails TestLocalWorktreesIgnoresInheritedGitRoutingVariables/{GIT_DIR,GIT_COMMON_DIR} and the matching internal/service subtests with the redirected response body printed. Reverting the grep site fails TestCitingDocumentsIgnoresInheritedGitRoutingVariables/{GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS,GIT_NOGLOB_PATHSPECS,GIT_DIR} with \"hid the citing page: got [], want [page.md]\". Reverting webRemoteURL to the post-parse check fails TestWebRemoteURLAdmitsOnlyHTTPAndHTTPS by name.\n\nWHAT MOVED UNDER THIS LANE, so you are not surprised by the diff. Merge 6bb01a86 landed the decision-records and signing-standing work and touched four of this lane's seven paths, so the lane was recut onto current main. I verified by hand that the merge survived: Publish.tsx, authority.ts, modalFocus.ts, records.ts and the six new ui tests are present, publishRefusal, decideSupersede, signingRefusal, buildRecordIndex and satisfier all resolve, and satisfier resolves inside the regenerated bundle. Then planner re-anchored the request at eb034253 and all four commits were rewritten onto it with the tree preserved byte for byte at f08ef41f.\n\nWHAT I DID NOT TAKE. internal/gitstore is redirectable the same way — cat-file returns another repository's object through a pinned --git-dir — and app.Open resolves through it. That is planner's separate request d2605fd7, gated on a threat-model ruling from hugh. The regressions here open the workspace before setting the variable so they isolate the five internal/app sites, and the comments say so.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head from a run I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached — cmd/gs 229.171s, internal/kernel 157.364s, internal/app 157.137s, internal/docset 99.737s, cmd/gitseq-mcp 92.132s. npm test 131 pass, 0 fail. gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0; git diff --check exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.\n\nDo not merge.","body":{"branch":"request/repo-remote-link","conditions":"Independent review of exact clean pushed head f6335179d5b8d0e908bf4cf0bf7211d7bd79d1be on request/repo-remote-link, citing all seven live artifacts standing at that head: 0aa1cf46 internal/app, 1694c953 internal/service, f289ce3f ui, ae4be00b internal/service/uidist, 081b44eb docs/reference/architecture.md, eb09d46a docs/reference/gs/serve.md, 03782557 docs/concepts/components.md. Governing request is planner's current-basis eb034253; my promise is 8abe2015. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions and file the verdict with gs review resting on all seven artifacts. SECURITY: judge whether every Git invocation behind LocalRepo and /v0/worktrees is now bound to the resolved repository, whether any inherited variable can still redirect the repository or silence the citation pathspec, and whether the raw-delimiter check closes the Go/browser divergence for every empty-delimiter form. Do not merge.","head":"f6335179d5b8d0e908bf4cf0bf7211d7bd79d1be","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}